11.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B2}

The relevant black group here is C1-C2 (the other black stones form separate groups that cannot be captured unconditionally). This group has exactly two liberties (B1 and B2). White's only forcing first move is therefore B2, which puts the group in atari. Black's only reply is B1 (connecting and adding the new liberty A1); white then answers at A1 and captures the three-stone group on the next move regardless of any intervening black plays elsewhere. No other first move by white forces capture of any black group against optimal defense. 

(The B3-B4 group has three liberties and cannot be captured unconditionally in a single sequence; A2 is already safe.)

10.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B1}

The black group (connected via A2-B3-B4-C2-C1) currently has exactly five liberties: A1, A3, A4, B1, B2. White's surrounding stones already control C3/C4/D1/D2, leaving only those five external points.

B1 is the only legal move that both (a) is not an immediate suicide and (b) begins a forcing sequence that removes liberties faster than Black can create two eyes. After White B1 the remaining liberties are A1/A3/A4/B2; every subsequent Black reply can be answered by White atari or direct filling (A1 or B2) that leaves Black with a single eye or none at all. All other candidate points are either illegal (A3, B2) or fail to force the capture against optimal Black defense (A1, A4, D3, etc.). Hence the sole first move that initiates a kill regardless of Black's replies is B1.

