2.text:
The C1-C2 chain has exactly two liberties (B1/B2), with C2 already reduced to one. Playing B2 captures only C2 (single stone); C1 immediately regains C2 as a liberty and is not left in atari. Black snaps back safely at B1. Symmetrically, B1 captures only C1 and permits the same snapback at B2.  

Neither reduces the full chain to a single liberty. Black can also answer either attempt with A3 (adds an edge liberty while threatening reconnection to A2/B3/B4) or leverage the intact D1/D2 wall + D5 ko for tempo. All other candidate points leave the chain at least one liberty or an escape route under optimal replies. No first move therefore forces unconditional capture.  
